<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qarnawu</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qarnaw</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qarnawu was the capital of the ancient South Arabian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-main">Kingdom of Ma'in</a>, in the al-Jawf valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. Its walled ruins, at the modern site of Ma'in, contain gates and temples, and Minaic inscriptions name it as the seat of the kings. It flourished from about the 6th to the 1st century BCE through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/incense">incense</a> trade.</p></div>
